# Build and run instructions

## Prerequisites
- Rust toolchain (stable). Check with: `rustc --version` and `cargo --version`.
- Windows target (msvc). The project is developed on Windows.

## Build (debug)
```
cargo build
```
Produces: `target/debug/whyedcode.exe`

## Build (release)
```
cargo build --release
```
Produces: `target/release/whyedcode.exe` (~3 MB)

## Install / replace the launcher binary
After a release build, copy the new binary over the root launcher:
```
copy target/release/whyedcode.exe whyedcode.exe
```
(On PowerShell: `Copy-Item target/release/whyedcode.exe whyedcode.exe -Force`)

## Run
```
.\whyedcode.exe
```
or from anywhere if `whyedcode.exe` (or `whyedcode.cmd`) is on PATH.

## Configuration
Config file: `~/.whyed/config.ini` (Windows: `%USERPROFILE%\.whyed\config.ini`).
Example:
```ini
[ai]
api = token-abc123
api_url = http://localhost:8080/v1

[app]
accent = orange
version = v2.0.12-dev

[history]
enabled = true
max_items = 100
save_path = ~/.whyed/history.json
```

## Notes
- The app expects a local AI server listening on the configured `api_url`.
- Default endpoint used by the client: `<api_url>/chat/completions`.
- If no server is running, the app prints a connection-refused error in Russian.
